ONE-LARGE-SPEED INTERVAL PEELER (codex S117b)

General lemma:
  If seed max is m and seed witness margin is alpha>1/n,
  then adding speed v is safe whenever
      v > m / (n*(alpha-1/n)).
  The proof only compares one connected seed-safe arc with one
  connected tooth of the new speed's danger comb.

LRC(n-1) corollary checked for n=4..14:
  alpha=1/(n-1) gives the sharp symbolic threshold v > (n-1)*m.

LRC14 generic seed from LRC13
  n=14, alpha=1/13, seed max m=13
  seed-safe arc length >= 1/1183
  strict threshold v > 169
  least integer v certified = 170
  tooth length at v0 = 1/1190
  arc > tooth? True

